🔹 Navigator.push
Adds (pushes) a new route (screen) on top of the stack.
The previous screen stays in memory.
You can go back with Navigator.pop(context).

🔹 Navigator.pushReplacement
Replaces the current screen with a new one.
The previous screen is removed from the stack.
You cannot go back to it with pop.

## SafeArea: Prevents UI from overlapping with the status bar, notches, etc.

Yes ✅ absolutely, you can use InkWell instead of GestureDetector.
Both can detect taps, but the difference is:
GestureDetector → detects gestures, but no visual feedback (no ripple effect).
InkWell → detects taps and shows a ripple effect (Material ink splash) by default

## SingleChildScrollView in Flutter is a scrollable widget that allows its single child to scroll when the content is larger than the available screen space.

## validate() ensures all form fields are correct before submitting.
Helps prevent invalid data from going forward.

## initState() runs once when the widget is first created.
Here, you are adding listeners to your text controllers:
_phoneController.addListener(_validateInput)
_emailController.addListener(_validateInput)
Purpose: Every time the user types in the phone or email field, _validateInput is called automatically.


## dispose() is called when the widget is removed from the widget tree.
You must dispose of your TextEditingControllers to free up memory and prevent memory leaks.
super.dispose() is called after your cleanup to complete the widget disposal.